  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Project to Support the Strengthening of Social Cohesion, the Prevention of Violent Extremism and the Fight against Transhumance-related Conflicts (Pro</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project is part of the collaboration between the Government of Benin, the Embassy of the Netherlands, the United Nations Development Program (UNDP) and local NGOs to strengthen the country&apos;s efforts to consolidate peace, promote social cohesion, and to prevent violent extremism. The project contributes to the implementation of Benin&apos;s strategy for the prevention of violent extremism, radicalisation and terrorism. Its purpose is to contribute to the achievement of equitable and inclusive access to efficient, transparent and accountable institutions and to a modern public administration, at all levels, in particular to justice that respects human rights, in a climate of peace and security, and the strengthening of national capacities for the peaceful conflict management and the prevention of violent extremism. The project is structured around three pillars: 1) social cohesion, 2) prevention of violent extremism, 3) fight against conflicts linked to transhumance.</narrative>
  </description>
